{"kind":"artifact","text":"cmd/gs as main carries it, at merge commit e677dd8f54f1380040e19a36a290f7a32f7841d5, which landed the reviewed-paths work approved by codex in 66e46023 and ratified in 4c64bd4d.\n\nWhat changed. The succession planner now derives its retirement set from artifacts whose commit is already in the world the merge is landing into, or is the reviewed candidate itself, so a live candidate for some other proposed head stays live and reviewable rather than being retired by a merge that never looked at it. And the authority check reads every artifact the approval rests on at the reviewed head, not the single one its body names, so a change spanning several paths can complete its own succession.\n\nThis replaces 867e6897, which gs merge published for this same commit and which was stale from birth. That is not a transcription error; it is a defect in the machinery, and it is recorded in the assert filed alongside this record. Briefly: the automation rests every successor on the merge receipt, the receipt rests on the approval, and the approval rests on the candidate artifacts that the same batch retires. Retirement is retroactive, so the successor is stale before it is read. The command then refuses on its own post-condition, which requires exactly one current and non-stale successor per published path, and exits non-zero after the merge has already landed.\n\nEverything else the run did was right, and it is worth saying so: fourteen predecessors retired, every supersession effective, including three of codex the old rule could not touch and the long-cited pointers 7463de51, 0d7b8dde and b67e9b56 that had been carried as debt for days because a cited retirement with no successor is refused. The new cross-actor authority and the cited-with-successor rule both did exactly what they were written to do on their first live run.\n\nIt rests on 9891ec40 at internal/gitstore, live and not stale, at a path this merge does not touch, rather than on the receipt.","body":{"commit":"e677dd8f54f1380040e19a36a290f7a32f7841d5","path":"cmd/gs"}}